 {:db/id "q-338082/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe235fa-bcf8-5953-9422-9db01e330fa5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338082/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338082/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338082/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-338082" :question/id #uuid "e8b12875-ae8a-5464-b1d4-8be3ec87c5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-338082" :question/problem "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+2y=x$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y=-5x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-5x,$ which is different from zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338082/ma-source-field/b416211afb1db3691dc69bd37b794a6a12159a613c3c04f5654bced2573a228d" "q-338082/ma-source-field/deb5193a499c69bf008c26eefe92820717b89d5197afe3617689f24203dd3b08" "q-338082/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
